{%- comment -%}
  Photos per metal on the product page (2026-10-12, owner: "when I change the material to rose
  gold, only the rose gold pictures should appear"). Shopify ties one photo to a variant; the
  other photos of a metal are marked by their alt text in Shopify admin, written exactly as an
  option value of the product, e.g. „розово злато“ or „14К розово злато“ (case does not matter).

  Prints "hide" when the photo's alt text is one of this product's option values and the
  selected variant does not have that value; prints nothing otherwise, so photos with no alt
  text or with any other text keep showing for every variant. Used by
  snippets/product-media-gallery.liquid and snippets/product-media-modal.liquid; Dawn's
  product-info.js then adds and removes photos itself when the variant changes.

  Accepts:
  - media: {Object} the product media
  - product: {Object} the product

  Usage:
  {%- capture cj_hide -%}{% render 'cj-metal-photo', media: media, product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cj_alt = media.alt | strip | downcase
  if cj_alt != blank and product
    assign cj_key = '|' | append: cj_alt | append: '|'
    assign cj_all = '|'
    for option in product.options_with_values
      for value in option.values
        assign cj_value = value | append: '' | strip | downcase
        assign cj_all = cj_all | append: cj_value | append: '|'
      endfor
    endfor
    if cj_all contains cj_key
      assign cj_selected = '|'
      for value in product.selected_or_first_available_variant.options
        assign cj_value = value | append: '' | strip | downcase
        assign cj_selected = cj_selected | append: cj_value | append: '|'
      endfor
      unless cj_selected contains cj_key
        echo 'hide'
      endunless
    endif
  endif
-%}
